<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns"><key id="title" for="node" attr.name="title" attr.type="string" /><key id="type" for="all" attr.name="type" attr.type="string" /><key id="summary" for="all" attr.name="summary" attr.type="string" /><key id="doc" for="node" attr.name="doc" attr.type="string" /><key id="page" for="node" attr.name="page" attr.type="string" /><key id="evidence" for="all" attr.name="evidence" attr.type="string" /><graph id="vedic-atlas" edgedefault="directed"><node id="root"><data key="title">Vedic literature · supplied collection</data><data key="type">root</data><data key="summary">An evidence-linked map of the supplied Veda, Upanishad, Purana, and practical-guide PDFs. Explore works, hymns, narratives, shared concepts, source editions, and every PDF page.</data></node><node id="family-vedas"><data key="title">Four Vedic traditions</data><data key="type">family</data><data key="summary">Hymns, ritual formulas, chants, and selected translations. The files have different scopes and sometimes overlap.</data></node><node id="family-upanishads"><data key="title">108 Upanishads</data><data key="type">family</data><data key="summary">The supplied Muktika-ordered collection, with the ten modern commentaries kept distinct from translations.</data></node><node id="family-puranas"><data key="title">18 named Puranas</data><data key="type">family</data><data key="summary">Narrative, devotional, cosmological, ritual, and pilgrimage material. Many supplied files are retellings or partial volumes.</data></node><node id="family-bonus"><data key="title">Practical guides</data><data key="type">family</data><data key="summary">The supplied Ayurveda, yoga, and Vastu guides, organized separately from the scriptural texts.</data></node><node id="family-concepts"><data key="title">Ideas &amp; recurring figures</data><data key="type">family</data><data key="summary">Navigation through shared names and themes. Textual mentions and editorial comparisons do not establish historical borrowing or identical doctrine.</data></node><node id="v-rigveda"><data key="title">Rigveda</data><data key="type">text</data><data key="summary">Ten books of hymns in the supplied English translation. All 1,028 observed HYMN headings are indexed; hymn names and occasional misspellings follow this file. A metrical glossary follows the hymns.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">1</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 1, "quote": "RIG VEDA - THE FIRST BOOK"}]</data></node><node id="v-samaveda"><data key="title">Samaveda</data><data key="type">text</data><data key="summary">Songs arranged for ritual chanting. The supplied Griffith preface describes verses drawn mainly from the Rigveda and rearranged for ritual. The 460 song groups below use the explicit hierarchy in the indexed draft compilation; a separate Stevenson translation is also supplied.</data><data key="doc">four-vedas-english-translation</data><data key="page">1176</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "four-vedas-english-translation", "page": 1176, "quote": "HYMNS OF THE SAMAVEDA"}]</data></node><node id="v-yajurveda"><data key="title">Yajurveda</data><data key="type">text</data><data key="summary">Two distinct supplied presentations: the 40-chapter Tulsi Ram translation, and Keith’s numbered Taittiriya passages in the Four Vedas compilation. Their section numbering and interpretive traditions are preserved separately.</data><data key="doc">yajurveda</data><data key="page">1</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "yajurveda", "page": 1, "quote": "YAJURVEDA"}]</data></node><node id="v-atharvaveda"><data key="title">Atharvaveda</data><data key="type">text</data><data key="summary">Whitney/Lanman volume I supplies books I–VII with critical commentary, 433 hymns under its Berlin numbering. Bloomfield’s supplied anthology adds selections from later books and explicitly says it covers about one third of the entire material.</data><data key="doc">atharvaveda</data><data key="page">11</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "atharvaveda", "page": 11, "quote": "Introduction.               Books I to VII"}]</data></node><node id="rv-b1"><data key="title">Rigveda · Book 1</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">191 observed hymn headings in this book.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">1</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 1, "quote": "RIG VEDA - THE FIRST BOOK"}]</data></node><node id="rv-1-1"><data key="title">RV 1.1 · Agni</data><data key="type">hymn</data><data key="summary">Hymn heading: Agni. Read the cited passage for the complete hymn.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">2</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 2, "quote": "HYMN I. Agni."}]</data></node><node id="rv-1-2"><data key="title">RV 1.2 · Vayu</data><data key="type">hymn</data><data key="summary">Hymn heading: Vayu. Read the cited passage for the complete hymn.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">2</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 2, "quote": "HYMN II. Vayu."}]</data></node><node id="rv-1-3"><data key="title">RV 1.3 · Asvins</data><data key="type">hymn</data><data key="summary">Hymn heading: Asvins. Read the cited passage for the complete hymn.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">2</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 2, "quote": "HYMN III. Asvins"}]</data></node><node id="rv-1-4"><data key="title">RV 1.4 · Indri</data><data key="type">hymn</data><data key="summary">Hymn heading: Indri. Read the cited passage for the complete hymn.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">3</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 3, "quote": "HYMN IV. Indri"}]</data></node><node id="rv-1-5"><data key="title">RV 1.5 · Indra</data><data key="type">hymn</data><data key="summary">Hymn heading: Indra. Read the cited passage for the complete hymn.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">3