ading: Agni. Read the cited passage for the complete hymn.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">619</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 619, "quote": "HYMN XI. Agni"}]</data></node><node id="rv-10-12"><data key="title">RV 10.12 · Agni</data><data key="type">hymn</data><data key="summary">Hymn heading: Agni. Read the cited passage for the complete hymn.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">620</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 620, "quote": "HYMN XII. Agni"}]</data></node><node id="rv-10-13"><data key="title">RV 10.13 · Havirdhanas</data><data key="type">hymn</data><data key="summary">Hymn heading: Havirdhanas. Read the cited passage for the complete hymn.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">621</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 621, "quote": "HYMN XIII Havirdhanas."}]</data></node><node id="rv-10-14"><data key="title">RV 10.14 · Yama and the ancestors</data><data key="type">hymn</data><data key="summary">A funeral hymn invoking Yama, the Fathers, and the path to those who have gone before.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">621</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 621, "quote": "HYMN XIV. Yama."}, {"doc": "rigveda", "page": 621, "quote": "1. HONOUR the King with thine oblations, Yama, Vivasvan's Son, who gathers"}]</data></node><node id="rv-10-15"><data key="title">RV 10.15 · Fathers</data><data key="type">hymn</data><data key="summary">Hymn heading: Fathers. Read the cited passage for the complete hymn.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">622</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 622, "quote": "HYMN XV. Fathers."}]</data></node><node id="rv-10-16"><data key="title">RV 10.16 · Agni</data><data key="type">hymn</data><data key="summary">Hymn heading: Agni. Read the cited passage for the complete hymn.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">624</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 624, "quote": "HYMN XVI. Agni."}]</data></node><node id="rv-10-17"><data key="title">RV 10.17 · Various Deities</data><data key="type">hymn</data><data key="summary">Hymn heading: Various Deities. Read the cited passage for the complete hymn.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">625</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 625, "quote": "HYMN XVII. Various Deities."}]</data></node><node id="rv-10-18"><data key="title">RV 10.18 · Funeral and return to life</data><data key="type">hymn</data><data key="summary">Funeral verses address death and the living, including the earth as shelter and the widow’s return to the living.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">626</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 626, "quote": "HYMN XVIII. Various Deities."}, {"doc": "rigveda", "page": 626, "quote": "1. Go hence, O Death, pursue thy special pathway apart from that which"}]</data></node><node id="rv-10-19"><data key="title">RV 10.19 · Waters or Cows</data><data key="type">hymn</data><data key="summary">Hymn heading: Waters or Cows. Read the cited passage for the complete hymn.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">627</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 627, "quote": "HYMN XIX. Waters or Cows."}]</data></node><node id="rv-10-20"><data key="title">RV 10.20 · Agni</data><data key="type">hymn</data><data key="summary">Hymn heading: Agni. Read the cited passage for the complete hymn.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">627</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 627, "quote": "HYMN XX. Agni."}]</data></node><node id="rv-10-21"><data key="title">RV 10.21 · Agni</data><data key="type">hymn</data><data key="summary">Hymn heading: Agni. Read the cited passage for the complete hymn.</data><data key="doc">rigveda</data><data key="page">628</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "rigveda", "page": 628, "quote": "HYMN XXI. Agni."}]</data></node><node