rishni dynasty</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Chapter navigation in the supplied Part III continuation: The Vrishni dynasty. Inclusive range may include the next chapter heading page.</data><data key="doc">brahmaand-purana</data><data key="page">168</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahmaand-purana", "page": 168, "quote": "CHAPTER SEVENTYONE The Vr›ni Dynasty Suta sara :—", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="p-brahmanda-ch-072"><data key="title">Brahmanda 72: Praise of the Lord: conclusion</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Chapter navigation in the supplied Part III continuation: Praise of the Lord: conclusion. Inclusive range may include the next chapter heading page.</data><data key="doc">brahmaand-purana</data><data key="page">190</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahmaand-purana", "page": 190, "quote": "CHAPTER SEVENTYTWO Praise of the Lord: Conclusion Suta said :-", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="p-brahmanda-ch-073"><data key="title">Brahmanda 73: The glory of Vishnu</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Chapter navigation in the supplied Part III continuation: The glory of Vishnu. Inclusive range may include the next chapter heading page.</data><data key="doc">brahmaand-purana</data><data key="page">209</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahmaand-purana", "page": 209, "quote": "CHAPTER SEVENTYTHREE Description of the Glory of Visnu Sita said :-", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="p-brahmanda-ch-074"><data key="title">Brahmanda 74: Royal dynasties</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Chapter navigation in the supplied Part III continuation: Royal dynasties. Inclusive range may include the next chapter heading page.</data><data key="doc">brahmaand-purana</data><data key="page">220</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahmaand-purana", "page": 220, "quote": "CHAPTER SEVENTYFOUR Royal Dynasties Suta said :—", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="p-scan-story-manu-shelters-the-growing-fish"><data key="title">Manu shelters the growing fish</data><data key="type">story</data><data key="summary">Manu protects a small fish, which repeatedly outgrows its containers. The revealed divine fish promises protection in a future dissolution.</data><data key="doc">matsyapurana-english</data><data key="page">21</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "matsyapurana-english", "page": 21, "quote": "reason Vignu adopted the form of a fish. We are also anxious to know", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="p-scan-story-the-flood-the-boat-and-cosmic-renewal"><data key="title">The flood, the boat and cosmic renewal</data><data key="type">story</data><data key="summary">The fish tells Manu the signs of destruction and the preparations by which living beings are to be preserved through the flood.</data><data key="doc">matsyapurana-english</data><data key="page">24</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "matsyapurana-english", "page": 24, "quote": "this boat to rescue the creation from such a calamity, placing in it", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="p-scan-story-prithu-milks-the-earth"><data key="title">Prithu milks the earth</data><data key="type">story</data><data key="summary">The narrative explains Prithu’s relation to the earth, which takes cow form, and the provision of nourishment for beings.</data><data key="doc">matsyapurana-english</data><data key="page">47</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "matsyapurana-english", "page": 47, "quote": "bling with fear, assumed the form of a cow and took to fight. -11-12.", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="p-scan-story-kacha-devayani-and-the-reviving-knowledge"><data key="title">Kacha, Devayani and the reviving knowledge</data><data key="type">story</data><data key="summary">Kacha learns from Shukra while repeated attacks by the Asuras test the teacher’s reviving power. The episode ends with mutual curses involving Devayani.</data><data key="doc">matsyapurana-english</data><data key="page">98</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "matsyapurana-english", "page": 98, "quote": "Kacha. -8-14.", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="p-scan-story-devayani-and-sharmishtha-at-the-well"><data key="title">Devayani and Sharmishtha at the well</data><data key="type">story</data><data key="summary">A quarrel between Devayani and Sharmishtha leads to Devayani’s fall into a well and rescue by Yayati; Shukra becomes involved in resolving the humiliation.</data><data key="doc">matsyapurana-english</data><data key="page">103</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "matsyapurana-english", "page": 104, "quote": "wards she threw the astonished and bewildered DevayAnt into a well and", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="p-scan-story-yayati-borrows-puru-s-youth"><data key="title">Yayati borrows Puru’s youth</data><data key="type">story</data><data key="summary">Struck with old age, Yayati asks his sons for an exchange. Puru accepts, and the narrative connects this action with his succession.</data><data key="doc">matsyapurana-english</data><data key="page">115</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "matsyapurana-english", "page": 116, "quote": "Yayâti then put the same proposal to his son, Puru, and said that by", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="p-scan-story-the-ten-incarnations-in-the-matsya-account"><data key="title">The ten incarnations in the Matsya account</data><data key="type">story</data><data key="summary">This long chapter connects Shukra’s curse and the conflict of gods and Asuras with an account of divine incarnations.</data><data key="doc">matsyapurana-english</data><data key="page">142</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "matsyapurana-english", "page": 142, "quote": "Note.- It means that Kasyapa was a partial incarnation of the Creator, whilst his", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="p-scan-story-parashurama-and-ganesha-s-broken-tusk"><data key="title">Parashurama and Ganesha’s broken tusk</data><data key="type">story</data><data key="summary">Parashurama reports his attempted entrance into Shiva’s realm, conflict with Ganesha, axe-blow to the tusk, and subsequent reconciliation.</data><data key="doc">brahmaand-purana</data><data key="page">10</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahmaand-purana", "page": 12, "quote": "axe was hurled by ine with great anger. His tusk was felled down", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="p-scan-story-jamadagni-s-murder-and-parashurama-s-return"><data key="title">Jamadagni’s murder and Parashurama’s return</data><data key="type">story</data><data key="summary">The sons of Kartavirya kill Jamadagni. Parashurama hears the account, returns and pursues vengeance.</data><data key="doc">brahmaand-purana</data><data key="page">13</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahmaand-purana", "page": 13, "quote": "saw the hermitage of Jamadagni on the way.", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="p-scan-story-sagara-s-sons-and-kapila"><data key="title">Sagara’s sons and Kapila</data><data key="type">story</data><data key="summary">Sagara’s sons, searching for the sacrificial horse, approach Kapila and meet destruction; the story explains the need for later rites and Ganga’s descent.</data><data key="doc">brahmaand-purana</data><data key="page">55</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahmaand-purana", "page": 55, "quote": "vicinity of sage Kapila.", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="p-scan-story-bhagiratha-brings-ganga-down"><data key="title">Bhagiratha brings Ganga down</data><data key="type">story</data><data key="summary">The descent of Ganga completes the sequence concerning Sagara’s descendants and the deliverance of his sons.</data><data key="doc">brahmaand-purana</data><data key="page">67</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahmaand-purana", "page": 70, "quote": "32. His son named Bhagiratha became very famous", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="p-scan-story-parashurama-and-the-land-reclaimed-from-the-sea"><data key="title">Parashurama and the land reclaimed from the sea</data><data key="type">story</data><data key="summary">After Varuna’s visit, Rama determines the land he is to reclaim from the sea, within the continuation of the Bhargava narrative.</data><data key="doc">brahmaand-purana</data><data key="page">79</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahmaand-purana", "page": 79, "quote": "Râma reclaims land from the sea", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="p-scan-story-music-within-a-purana"><data key="title">Music within a Purana</data><data key="type">story</data><data key="summary">Two chapters interrupt the genealogical sequence with a dissertation on music, notes and musical embellishments.</data><data key="doc">brahmaand-purana</data><data key="page">92</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahmaand-purana", "page": 92, "quote": "A dissertation on Music", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda"><data key="title">Ayurvedic Home Remedies</data><data key="type">text</data><data key="summary">A supplied practical booklet with an index and 25 ingredient entries. This map catalogs the subjects and page locations; the traditional treatment claims are not evaluated here.</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">1</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 1, "quote": "INDEX S.NO. Page Forew ord i Instructions ii 1. Adrak/Scnth 1 2. Ajvain 2 3. Anar 3 4. Amla 4 5. Dalchini 5 6. Dhania 6 7. Elaichi 7 8. Ghee 8 9. Haldi 9 10. Hing 10 11. Jayphal 11 12. Jeer a 12 13. Kalimirach 13 14. Kar"}]</data></node><node id="b-vastu"><data key="title">Practical Vastu for Homes and Businesses</data><data key="type">text</data><data key="summary">A supplied modern advisory guide to existing homes, shops and offices, presented separately from scripture. Its 44 pages cover spatial principles, direction readings, layouts and correction checklists.</data><data key="doc">practical-vastu-professional-guide-1</data><data key="page">1</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "practical-vastu-professional-guide-1", "page": 1, "quote": "Practical Vastu for Existing Homes, Shops and Offices Practical Vastu for Homes &amp; Businesses Ancient Principles, Modern Fixes and Simple Remedies for Daily Life A practical Vastu guide for homes, shops and offices rooted"}]</data></node><node id="b-yoga"><data key="title">Common Yoga Protocol</data><data key="type">text</data><data key="summary">A supplied illustrated Ministry of Ayush yoga guide. The 51-page scan includes introductory material, loosening practices, postures, breathing practices and the beginning of Dhyana. Topics listed later in its contents are not present at the end of this supplied file.</data><data key="doc">common-yoga-aasana-englishebook</data><data key="page">1</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "common-yoga-aasana-englishebook", "page": 5, "quote": "COMMON YOGA PROTOCOL Ministry of Ayush, Government of India What is Yoga?"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-1"><data key="title">Adrak / Sonth (ginger)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 1 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Adrak / Sonth (ginger).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">5</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 5, "quote": "A drak/ Sonth ( Zingiber officinale Rose., A rdraka/Sunthi)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-2"><data key="title">Ajvain</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 2 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Ajvain.</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">6</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 6, "quote": "ATYAIN (Trachyspremum amrni Spragne, Yavani)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-3"><data key="title">Anar (pomegranate)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 3 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Anar (pomegranate).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">7</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 7, "quote": "ANAR ( Punica granntum Linn., Dadima)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-4"><data key="title">Amla</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 4 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Amla.</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">8</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 8, "quote": "AMLA (Emblica officinalis Gaertn., Amalaki)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-5"><data key="title">Dalchini (cinnamon)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 5 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Dalchini (cinnamon).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">9</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 9, "quote": "DALCHINI ( Cinnamomum zeylam cum Blume ,Tvak)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-6"><data key="title">Dhania (coriander)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 6 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Dhania (coriander).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">10</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 10, "quote": "DHANIA ( Conundrum sativum L in n ., Dhanyaka)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-7"><data key="title">Elaichi (cardamom)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 7 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Elaichi (cardamom).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">11</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 11, "quote": "ELAICHI ( Elettarin cnrdnmomum Maton, Ela)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-8"><data key="title">Ghee (clarified butter)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 8 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Ghee (clarified butter).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">12</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 12, "quote": "GHEE (Clarified Butter)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-9"><data key="title">Haldi (turmeric)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 9 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Haldi (turmeric).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">13</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 13, "quote": "HALDI {Curcuma longa Linn., Haridra)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-10"><data key="title">Hing (asafoetida)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 10 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Hing (asafoetida).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">14</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 14, "quote": "HING (Ferula narthex Boiss., Hingu)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-11"><data key="title">Jayphal (nutmeg)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 11 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Jayphal (nutmeg).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">15</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 15, "quote": "TAYPHAL (Myristica fragm ns Houtt., Jatiphala)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-12"><data key="title">Jeera (cumin)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 12 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Jeera (cumin).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">16</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 16, "quote": "1EERA ( Cuminum cyminum Linn., jiraka)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-13"><data key="title">Kalimirach (black pepper)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 13 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Kalimirach (black pepper).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">17</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 17, "quote": "KALIM IRACH ( Piper nigrum Linn., M aricha)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-14"><data key="title">Karela (bitter gourd)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 14 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Karela (bitter gourd).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">18</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 18, "quote": "KARELA (M omordica charantin Linn., Karavellaka)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-15"><data key="title">Lahsun (garlic)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 15 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Lahsun (garlic).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">19</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 19, "quote": "LAHSUN (.Allium sativum Linn., Rasona)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-16"><data key="title">Laung (clove)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 16 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Laung (clove).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">20</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 20, "quote": "LAUNG ( Syzygium aromaticum (L.) Merr &amp; Perry, Lavanga)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-17"><data key="title">Madhu (honey)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 17 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Madhu (honey).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">21</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 21, "quote": "M A PH U f Honey)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-18"><data key="title">Methi (fenugreek)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 18 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Methi (fenugreek).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">22</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 22, "quote": "METHI ( Trigonellafoenum -graecum Linn., Methika)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-19"><data key="title">Nariyal (coconut)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 19 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Nariyal (coconut).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">23</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 23, "quote": "NARIYAL ( Cocos nucifern Linn., Narikela)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-20"><data key="title">Neem</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 20 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Neem.</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">24</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 24, "quote": "NEEM ( Azadirachtn indica A. juss., Nimba)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-21"><data key="title">Nimbu (lemon)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 21 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Nimbu (lemon).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">25</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 25, "quote": "NIM BU (Citrus limon Linn., Nimbu)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-22"><data key="title">Pyaj (onion)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 22 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Pyaj (onion).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">26</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 26, "quote": "PYAT ( Allium cepa Linn., Palandu)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-23"><data key="title">Pippali (long pepper)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 23 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Pippali (long pepper).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">27</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 27, "quote": "PIPPALI (Piper longum Linn., Pippali)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-24"><data key="title">Saunf (fennel)</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 24 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Saunf (fennel).</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">28</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 28, "quote": "SAUNF (Foeniculum vulgare Mill., Shatapushpa)"}]</data></node><node id="b-ayurveda-topic-25"><data key="title">Tulsi</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Ingredient entry 25 in the supplied home-remedies booklet: Tulsi.</data><data key="doc">ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook</data><data key="page">29</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "ayurvedic-home-remediesenglishebook", "page": 29, "quote": "TULSI (Ocimum sanctum , Tulasi)"}]</data></node><node id="b-vastu-page-1"><data key="title">Practical Vastu for Homes and Businesses — cover</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Source topic: Practical Vastu for Homes and Businesses — cover.</data><data key="doc">practical-vastu-professional-guide-1</data><data key="page">1</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "practical-vastu-professional-guide-1", "page": 1, "quote": "Practical Vastu for Existing Homes, Shops and Offices Practical Vastu for Homes &amp; Businesses"}]</data></node><node id="b-vastu-page-2"><data key="title">Important Note and How to Use This Guide</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Source topic: Important Note and How to Use This Guide.</data><data key="doc">practical-vastu-professional-guide-1</data><data key="page">2</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "practical-vastu-professional-guide-1", "page": 2, "quote": "Practical Vastu for Existing Homes, Shops and Offices Important Note and How to Use This Guide Read this before applying any recommendation."}]</data></node><node id="b-vastu-page-3"><data key="title">Path Through This Guide</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Source topic: Path Through This Guide.</data><data key="doc">practical-vastu-professional-guide-1</data><data key="page">3</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "practical-vastu-professional-guide-1", "page": 3, "quote": "Practical Vastu for Existing Homes, Shops and Offices Path Through This Guide Begin with the spiritual foundation, then move into practical corrections."}]</data></node><node id="b-vastu-page-4"><data key="title">Vastu and the Hindu Way of Living</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Source topic: Vastu and the Hindu Way of Living.</data><data key="doc">practical-vastu-professional-guide-1</data><data key="page">4</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "practical-vastu-professional-guide-1", "page": 4, "quote": "Practical Vastu for Existing Homes, Shops and Offices Vastu and the Hindu Way of Living Why many Hindu families feel emotionally connected to Vastu."}]</data></node><node id="b-vastu-page-5"><data key="title">Ancient Vastu Principles in Simple Language</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Source topic: Ancient Vastu Principles in Simple Language.</data><data key="doc">practical-vastu-professional-guide-1</data><data key="page">5</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "practical-vastu-professional-guide-1", "page": 5, "quote": "Practical Vastu for Existing Homes, Shops and Offices Ancient Vastu Principles in Simple Language The knowledge system behind the rules."}]</data></node><node id="b-vastu-page-6"><data key="title">Quick Start: Compass Reading for Existing Properties</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Source topic: Quick Start: Compass Reading for Existing Properties.</data><data key="doc">practical-vastu-professional-guide-1</data><data key="page">6</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "practical-vastu-professional-guide-1", "page": 6, "quote": "Practical Vastu for Existing Homes, Shops and Offices Quick Start: Compass Reading for Existing Properties A simple repeatable method for non-experts."}]</data></node><node id="b-vastu-page-7"><data key="title">Vastu Zones in Plain English</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Source topic: Vastu Zones in Plain English.</data><data key="doc">practical-vastu-professional-guide-1</data><data key="page">7</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "practical-vastu-professional-guide-1", "page": 7, "quote": "Practical Vastu for Existing Homes, Shops and Offices Vastu Zones in Plain English Translate traditional zones into daily use decisions."}]</data></node><node id="b-vastu-page-8"><data key="title">The Existing-Property Approach</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Source topic: The Existing-Property Approach.</data><data key="doc">practical-vastu-professional-guide-1</data><data key="page">8</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "practical-vastu-professional-guide-1", "page": 8, "quote": "Practical Vastu for Existing Homes, Shops and Offices The Existing-Property Approach Fix what you can without demolition first."}]</data></node><node id="b-vastu-page-9"><data key="title">Toilet Direction Explained Clearly</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Source topic: Toilet Direction Explained Clearly.</data><data key="doc">practical-vastu-professional-guide-1</data><data key="page">9</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "practical-vastu-professional-guide-1", "page": 9, "quote": "Practical Vastu for Existing Homes, Shops and Offices Toilet Direction Explained Clearly Why northeast toilets are avoided and what better placement means."}]</data></node><node id="b-vastu-page-10"><data key="title">Priorities for Homes, Shops and Offices</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Source topic: Priorities for Homes, Shops and Offices.</data><data key="doc">practical-vastu-professional-guide-1</data><data key="page">10</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "practical-vastu-professional-guide-1", "page": 10, "quote": "Practical Vastu for Existing Homes, Shops and Offices Priorities for Homes, Shops and Offices Where to begin when everything looks important."}]</data></node><node id="b-vastu-page-11"><data key="title">Mistake 1: Toilet in the Northeast</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Source topic: Mistake 1: Toilet in the Northeast.</data><data key="doc">practical-vastu-professional-guide-1</data><data key="page">11</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "practical-vastu-professional-guide-1", "page": 11, "quote": "Practical Vastu for Existing Homes, Shops and Offices Mistake 1: Toilet in the Northeast Understand the concern, the principle behind it and the practical correction."}]</data></node><node id="b-vastu-page-12"><data key="title">Fix Plan: Toilet in the Northeast</data><data key="type">section</data><data key="summary">Source topic: Fix Plan: Toilet in the Northeast.</data><data key="doc">pra