ed section explicitly names this narrative or topic in its heading. Compare the passages; the link does not establish borrowing or doctrinal identity.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 6, "quote": "3.4.11 Description of Yaduvansh and the Tale of SahastrArjuna Yayati’s eldest son Yadu had four sons- Sahastrajit, Kroshtu, Nala and Nahush. Sahastrajit had a son Shatajit who had three sons Haihaya, Hehaya and Venuhaya. Lineage of Haihaya grew as- Dha"}]</data></edge><edge id="e683" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-3-5-3" target="motif-krishna-cycle"><data key="type">shared narrative</data><data key="summary">The supplied section explicitly names this narrative or topic in its heading. Compare the passages; the link does not establish borrowing or doctrinal identity.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 9, "quote": "3.5.3 Incarnation of Lord Krshna Vasudev, the son of Shoorsen was married to Devaki, the daughter of Devak. On that occasion of their marriage, Devaki’s cousin Kansa was driving their chariot. At that time, a celestial voic"}]</data></edge><edge id="e684" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-3-5-5" target="motif-krishna-cycle"><data key="type">shared narrative</data><data key="summary">The supplied section explicitly names this narrative or topic in its heading. Compare the passages; the link does not establish borrowing or doctrinal identity.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 10, "quote": "3.5.5 Killing of Putana and Salvation of other Demons When Vasudev was released from the prison, Nand visited Mathura on some official trip. He also came to see Vasudev. Vasudev greeted him for the birth of a son and instructed him to return to"}]</data></edge><edge id="e685" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-11-1533" target="motif-krishna-cycle"><data key="type">shared narrative</data><data key="summary">The supplied section explicitly names this narrative or topic in its heading. Compare the passages; the link doe