 his meditation. He told Upamanyu about his desire and requ"}]</data></edge><edge id="e708" source="p-shiv-maha-purana-2-5-5-2" target="motif-krishna-cycle"><data key="type">shared narrative</data><data key="summary">The supplied section explicitly names this narrative or topic in its heading. Compare the passages; the link does not establish borrowing or doctrinal identity.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "shiv-maha-purana-2", "page": 32, "quote": "5.5.2 Sri Krshna Does Penance Sri Krishna then proceeded to do his penance after getting initiated by Upamanyu with the mantra - Om Namah Shivay. He did a tremendous penance for fifteen months by standing on his toe. In"}]</data></edge><edge id="e709" source="p-shrimad-bhagwat-puran-16-8-2" target="motif-gajendra"><data key="type">shared narrative</data><data key="summary">The supplied section explicitly names this narrative or topic in its heading. Compare the passages; the link does not establish borrowing or doctrinal identity.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "shrimad-bhagwat-puran", "page": 30, "quote": "16.8.2 Tale of Gajendra, the elephant and Grah, the crocodile King Parikshit asked, \"Munivar, God had salve Gajendra, in His Hari incarnation. I wish to hear this tale.\" Shukdev says, \" O king, in Tamas Manvantara, God had appeared as Hari and saved Ga"}]</data></edge><edge id="e710" source="p-vamana-puran-6-22-6" target="motif-gajendra"><data key="type">shared narrative</data><data key="summary">The supplied section explicitly names this narrative or topic in its heading. Compare the passages; the link does not establish borrowing or doctrinal identity.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vamana-puran", "page": 41, "quote": "6.22.6 Gajendra and the Crocodile Sage Narad requests Pulastya to describe how Gajendra managed to release itself from the jaws of the crocodile. Pulastya says- \"There lived a crocodile in a reservoir near Trikut Mountain. O"}]</data></edge><edge id="e711" source="p-brahma-vaivart-p