link does not establish borrowing or doctrinal identity.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "shiv-maha-purana-2", "page": 5, "quote": "5.2.145 Battle Between Lord Shiva and Andhak Andhak had become so arrogant that once, he even dared to dishonour his own mother-Parvati, who at that time was living at the Mandarachal mountain. Shiva became very furious with him. Andha"}]</data></edge><edge id="e754" source="p-linga-purana-17-4-10" target="motif-jalandhara"><data key="type">shared narrative</data><data key="summary">The supplied section explicitly names this narrative or topic in its heading. Compare the passages; the link does not establish borrowing or doctrinal identity.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "linga-purana", "page": 21, "quote": "17.4.10 Killing of Jalandhar The Sages requested Sutji to reveal how Lord Shiva had killed the notorious demon-- Jalandhar. Sutji narrated the following tale--- There was a demon named Jalandhar. He had manifested from"}]</data></edge><edge id="e755" source="p-shrimad-bhagwat-puran-16-10-11" target="motif-jalandhara"><data key="type">shared narrative</data><data key="summary">The supplied section explicitly names this narrative or topic in its heading. Compare the passages; the link does not establish borrowing or doctrinal identity.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "shrimad-bhagwat-puran", "page": 46, "quote": "16.10.11 Migration to Vrindavana The uprooted Arjun trees fell with thundering sound. All the people shivered with fear and felt as if lightning had struck somewhere. All the elders including Nand met together and discussed"}]</data></edge><edge id="e756" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-12-3844" target="motif-jalandhara"><data key="type">shared narrative</data><data key="summary">The supplied section explicitly names this narrative or topic in its heading. Compare the passages; the link does not establish borrowing or doctrinal identity.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 12, "quote": "M