ata key="evidence">[{"doc": "shiv-maha-purana-2", "page": 9, "quote": "5.3.10 Bhairav Gets Liberated from his Sin Bhairav who was created by lord Shiva from his third eye, had severed one of the five heads of Lord Brahma on the instruction of lord Shiva. Now Brahmaji was left with only four heads. Carry"}]</data></edge><edge id="e770" source="p-kurma-puran-12-33" target="motif-nandi"><data key="type">shared narrative</data><data key="summary">The supplied section explicitly names this narrative or topic in its heading. Compare the passages; the link does not establish borrowing or doctrinal identity.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "kurma-puran", "page": 34, "quote": "12.33Nandi There used to be a sage named Shilada. He was righteous and learned in the shastras. To obtain a son, Shilada began to pray to shiva. The tapasya went on for a thousand years and shiva appea"}]</data></edge><edge id="e771" source="p-linga-purana-17-2-13" target="motif-nandi"><data key="type">shared narrative</data><data key="summary">The supplied section explicitly names this narrative or topic in its heading. Compare the passages; the link does not establish borrowing or doctrinal identity.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "linga-purana", "page": 13, "quote": "17.2.13 Shilad’s Impossible Demand Once, Shilad did an austere penance to please Indra. He was desirous of begetting a son. When Indra appeared he requested him to bless him with a son who was self-born as well as deathless."}]</data></edge><edge id="e772" source="p-linga-purana-17-3-4" target="motif-nandi"><data key="type">shared narrative</data><data key="summary">The supplied section explicitly names this narrative or topic in its heading. Compare the passages; the link does not establish borrowing or doctrinal identity.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "linga-purana", "page": 14, "quote": "17.3.4 Manifestation of Lord Nandishwar Shilad did a tremendous penance to please Lord Shiva. His penance continued for thousands of year. At last, Lord Shiva appeared before him and said--\"I am extremely pleased by you devotion."}]</data></edge><edge id="e773" source="p-shiv-maha-purana-2-5-3-9" target="motif-nandi"><data key="type">shared narrative</data><data key="summary">The supplied section explicitly names this narrative or topic in its heading. Compare the passages; the link does not establish borrowing or doctrinal identity.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "shiv-maha-purana-2", "page": 9, "quote": "5.3.9 Nandikeshwar While describing about the incarnation of Nandikeshwar Sutji says- Sage Shilad did a tremendous penance to please lord Shiva with an aspiration to have a son. Lord Shiva appeared before him"}]</data></edge><edge id="e774" source="p-shiv-maha-purana-2-5-7-22" target="motif-nandi"><data key="type">shared narrative</data><data key="summary">The supplied section explicitly names this narrative or topic in its heading. Compare the passages; the link does not establish borrowing or doctrinal identity.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "shiv-maha-purana-2", "page": 47, "quote": "5.7.22 SanatKumar Receive Shiva-Gyan from Nandi The sages thanked Vayudeva for giving the knowledge of Gyan-Yoga. The next day, they took bath in river Saraswati and performed their worship and rituals. After that they proceeded towards K"}]</data></edge><edge id="e775" source="p-brahma-vaivart-puran-9-12" target="motif-yayati"><data key="type">shared narrative</data><data key="summary">The supplied section explicitly names this narrative or topic in its heading. Compare the passages; the link does not establish borrowing or doctrinal identity.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahma-vaivart-puran", "page": 11, "quote": "9.12 Yayati In the lunar dynasty, there was born a powerful king named Nahusha. He married Viraja and they had six sons named Yati, Yajati, Samyati, Ayati, Yati, and Suyati. Yati became a hermit. So alt"}]</data></edge><edge id="e776" source="p-padma-puran-2-2-2" target="motif-ya