": "OCR"}]</data></edge><edge id="e866" source="p-brahmanda-ch-053" target="p-brahmanda-ch-056"><data key="type">narrative-sequence</data><data key="summary">The destruction of Sagara’s sons belongs to the narrative sequence completed by the descent of Ganga.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahmaand-purana", "page": 55, "quote": "CHAPTER FIFTYTHREE The destruction of the sons of Sagara Jarmini Said :", "extraction": "OCR"}, {"doc": "brahmaand-purana", "page": 67, "quote": "CHAPTER FIFTYSIX The Descent of Gangā Jarmini Said :", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></edge><edge id="e867" source="p-brahmanda-ch-061" target="p-brahmanda-ch-062"><data key="type">continuation</data><data key="summary">The discussion of music continues into the following chapter on the science of music.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahmaand-purana", "page": 92, "quote": "CHAPTER SIXTYONE A dissertation on Music Suta said :", "extraction": "OCR"}, {"doc": "brahmaand-purana", "page": 100, "quote": "CHAPTER SIXTYTWO The Science of Music 1. After knowing the views of earlier teachers, I shall", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></edge><edge id="e868" source="p-matsya-ch-049" target="p-matsya-ch-271"><data key="type">related-genealogy</data><data key="summary">The main-body Paurava genealogy and appendix translations of future dynasties form complementary genealogical reading routes in this edition.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "matsyapurana-english", "page": 164, "quote": "CHAPTER XLIX. Puru was the father of the most illustrious Janamejaya who begot Prâchitvata and ruled in the Fast, and gave his name to the Eastern", "extraction": "OCR"}, {"doc": "matsyapurana-english", "page": 407, "quote": "CHAPTER COLXXI. Rigis said:-O Sûta, you have described to us the dynasty of Puru, along with the future kings in that dynasty. Now tell us about those", "extraction": "OCR"}]</data></edge><edge id="e869" source="v-samaveda" target="concept-soma"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Ed