" target="concept-vishnu"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahma-puran", "page": 4, "quote": "1.3.8 Reason for holding the Conch White colour and sound are the main virtues of the conch. Through the colour of the conch, God Vishnu teaches us to follow the path of the truth. The sound is like a warning call that is if"}]</data></edge><edge id="e5417" source="p-brahma-puran-1-3-10" target="concept-vishnu"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahma-puran", "page": 5, "quote": "1.3.10 Why does Lord Vishnu hold a Mace? Mace is a weapon that shows and dares for the physical strength. It was used by the fighters to demonstrate their strength. Among all the ancient weapons, mace was the main. It application i"}]</data></edge><edge id="e5418" source="p-brahma-puran-1-3-11" target="concept-vishnu"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahma-puran", "page": 5, "quote": "1.3.11 Why is Garuda (Eagle) the Vehicle of Vishnu? Garuda (eagle) is said to be the king of the birds. It is the fearest of bird. Thus God is assuring his devotees to be fearless, because if any calamity befell them, he will reach them in no"}]</data></edge><edge id="e5419" source="p-brahma-puran-1-3-11" target="concept-devotion"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahma-puran", "page": 5, "quote": "1.3.11 Why is Garuda (Eagle) the Vehicle of Vishnu? Garuda (eagle) is said to be the king of the birds. It is the fearest of bird. Thus God is assuring his devotees to be fearless, because if any calamity befell them, he will reach them in no"}]</data></edge><edge id="e5420" source="p-brahma-puran-1-4" target="concept-devi"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahma-puran", "page": 5, "quote": "1.4 Goddess Laxmi This chapter contains 3 sections:"}]</data></edge><edge id="e5421" source="p-brahma-puran-1-4-1" target="concept-vishnu"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahma-puran", "page": 5, "quote": "1.4.1 Why Goddess Laxmi presses the feet of God? Goddess Lakshmi presents an example of an ideal spouse before the world.The supreme duty of a woman is described in the service of her husband. Second aspect of the message is for the people"}]</data></edge><edge id="e5422" source="p-brahma-puran-1-4-1" target="concept-devi"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahma-puran", "page": 5, "quote": "1.4.1 Why Goddess Laxmi presses the feet of God? Goddess Lakshmi presents an example of an ideal spouse before the world.The supreme duty of a woman is described in the service of her husband. Second aspect of the message is for the people"}]</data></edge><edge id="e5423" source="p-brahma-puran-1-4-1" target="concept-devotion"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "brahma-puran", "page": 5, "quote": "1.4.1 Why Goddess Laxmi presses the feet of God? Goddess Lakshmi presents an example of an ideal spouse before the world.The supreme duty of a woman is described in the service of her husband. Second aspect of the message is for the people"}]</data></edge><edge id="e5424" source="p-brahma-puran-1-4-2" target="concept-vi