-purana", "page": 27, "quote": "8.9 Rituals Pertaining to Last Rites This section contains 4 sections as follows:"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6171" source="p-varaha-purana-8-9-1" target="concept-sacrifice"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "varaha-purana", "page": 27, "quote": "8.9.1 Last Rites: Pitra Yagya Prithvi requested lord Varaha to define the meaning of 'Pitra' yagya(rituals pertaining to last rite) and it's significance. Lord Varaha replied-\"Sage Nimi was the first person to perform th"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6172" source="p-varaha-purana-8-9-3" target="concept-sacrifice"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "varaha-purana", "page": 28, "quote": "8.9.3 Last Rites: The Flawed Shraddh and its Prevention Prithvi requested Lord Varaha to describe about the mistakes committed during shraddh rituals and how they could be prevented--"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6173" source="p-varaha-purana-8-9-4" target="concept-creation"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "varaha-purana", "page": 29, "quote": "8.9.4 Last Rites: Preparation of ‘Madhupark’ While describing the method of preparing Madhupark, Lord Varaha told Prithvi--\"Madhupark\" manifested from the right half of my body at the time when the process of creation began. This is th"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6174" source="p-varaha-purana-8-9-4" target="concept-sacrifice"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "varaha-purana", "page": 29, "quote": "8.9.4 Last Rites: Preparation of ‘Madhupark’ While describing the method of preparing Madhupark, Lord Varaha told Prithvi--\"Madhupark\" manifested from the right half of my body at the time when the process of creation began. This is th"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6175" source="p-varaha-purana-8-10-2" target="concept-karma"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "varaha-purana", "page": 30, "quote": "8.10.2 Karma Vipak Karma Vipak means the fruits one reaps according to his or her Karma. While continuing with the description of various aspects of hell, Nachiketa told the assembled sages--At yamapuri, Chitr"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6176" source="p-varaha-purana-8-10-4" target="concept-moksha"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "varaha-purana", "page": 30, "quote": "8.10.4 Liberation from Sins Narad asked Yamaraj about the reason why joy was so elusive to human beings. He also wanted to know about the reasons for man's sorrows. Yamaraj replied---Man's destiny is defined by his own"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6177" source="p-varaha-purana-8-11-1" target="concept-yoga"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "varaha-purana", "page": 31, "quote": "8.11.1 Gokarneshwar The famous battle of 'Tarakamaya' had ended. The deities after having defeated the demons had once again regained the control of heaven. Lord Brahma being satisfied with the postive outcome"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6178" source="p-varaha-purana-8-11-2" target="concept-vishnu"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "varaha-purana", "page": 32, "quote": "8.11.2 The Means of Vishnu Realization Once, Sage Agastya narrate