ry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "varaha-purana", "page": 34, "quote": "8.11.7 Jambudveepa Dwelling upon the prominent islands, Lord Shiva told the assembled sages---\"Jambudweepa is spread in the area of one lakh yojan and it consists of numerous Janapadads. It is inhabited by 'si"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6191" source="p-varaha-purana-8-11-9" target="concept-shiva"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "varaha-purana", "page": 35, "quote": "8.11.9 Kusha Dweepa This island is twice the area of Shak dweepa. There are seven prominent mountain ranges in this island which are known as 'Kula Parvatas'--- Kumud, Unnat, Drona, Kank, Isha, Mahish and Manda"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6192" source="p-varaha-purana-8-11-11" target="concept-shiva"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "varaha-purana", "page": 35, "quote": "8.11.11 Shalmali Dweepa \"It is double the area of Kraunch dweepa and covers the 'clarified-butter' ocean from all sides. There are seven prominent mountains as well as seven rivers in this island.\" This way Lord Sh"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6193" source="p-varaha-purana-8-11-12" target="concept-shiva"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "varaha-purana", "page": 35, "quote": "8.11.12 Trishakti Describing the reason behind the manifestation of 'TriShakti' (Three goddesses manifesting from the bodies of Brahma Vishnu and Shiva), Lord Varah told Prithvi--- There lived a mighty demon"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6194" source="p-varaha-purana-8-11-12" target="concept-vishnu"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "varaha-purana", "page": 35, "quote": "8.11.12 Trishakti Describing the reason behind the manifestation of 'TriShakti' (Three goddesses manifesting from the bodies of Brahma Vishnu and Shiva), Lord Varah told Prithvi--- There lived a mighty demon"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6195" source="p-varaha-purana-8-11-12" target="concept-devi"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "varaha-purana", "page": 35, "quote": "8.11.12 Trishakti Describing the reason behind the manifestation of 'TriShakti' (Three goddesses manifesting from the bodies of Brahma Vishnu and Shiva), Lord Varah told Prithvi--- There lived a mighty demon"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6196" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-1-1" target="concept-vishnu"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 2, "quote": "3.1.1 Introduction and Origin of the Universe from Basic Elements Sage Parashar, the exponent of Vishnu Puraan had narrated this grand treatise to Maitreya. Sage Suta inherited it from Maitreya. The text presented here is a narration by Suta. Suta says- On"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6197" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-1-1" target="concept-creation"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 2, "quote": "3.1.1 Introduction and Origin of the Universe from Basic Elements Sage Parashar, the exponent of Vishnu Puraan had narrated this grand treatise to Maitreya. Sage Suta inherited it from Maitreya. The text presented here is a narration by Suta. Suta says- On"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6198" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-1-2" target="concept-moksha"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 3, "quote": "3.1.2 Birth of Brahma and Salvation of Earth by Varaha At the end of the previous Kalpa, when Brahma awakened from his long slumber, he saw all the worlds devoid of everything. With a desire to salve the earth from the depth of unfathomable inun"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6199" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-1-4" target="concept-creation"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 4, "quote": "3.1.4 Birth of Prajapatis and their Progeny At one point, the process of creation got saturated and no increase took place in the number of living beings. Then, with a desire of continuing the creation, Lord created nine sages from Hi"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6200" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-1-5" target="concept-shiva"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 5, "quote": "3.1.5 Creation of Rudra and Omnipresence of Laxmi In the beginning of Kalpa when Brahma was thinking about a son, who would be like him in virtues, a boy with reddish-blue body appeared in his lap. Brahma addressed the boy with names like R"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6201" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-1-5" target="concept-creation"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 5, "quote": "3.1.5 Creation of Rudra and Omnipresence of Laxmi In the beginning of Kalpa when Brahma was thinking about a son, who would be like him in virtues, a boy with reddish-blue body appeared in his lap. Brahma addressed the boy with names like R"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6202" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-1-6" target="concept-sacrifice"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 6, "quote": "3.1.6 Dhruv’s Migration to the Forest Swayambhu Manu had two sons- Priyavrata and Utaanpaad. Utaanpaad had two wives- Suruchi and Suniti. Suruchi had a son- Uttam while Suniti had also a son- Dhruv. King Utaanpaad loved Suruchi"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6203" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-1-9" target="concept-sacrifice"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 10, "quote": "3.1.9 Birth of Prachin Barhi Worship of God by Prachetas King Prithu had two sons- Antardhaan and Vaadi who were very religious minded themselves. Antardhaan’s wife Shikhandi gave birth to Ivirdhaan. Prachin Barhi was the son of Ivirdhaan and his"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6204" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-1-14" target="concept-vishnu"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 15, "quote": "3.1.14 Appearance of the Lord As soon as Prahlad began to pray the Lord, his Naagpaash broke and the mountains that the demons had thrown into the sea also lightened up causing great relief for Prahlad. Lord Vishnu appea"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6205" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-1-14" target="concept-devotion"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 15, "quote": "3.1.14 Appearance of the Lord As soon as Prahlad began to pray the Lord, his Naagpaash broke and the mountains that the demons had thrown into the sea also lightened up causing great relief for Prahlad. Lord Vishnu appea"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6206" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-1-16" target="concept-sacrifice"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 16, "quote": "3.1.16 The Description of Universal Order When the great sages crowned Prithu as the king of the entire earth, Brahma had also divided the kingdoms. Thus, Brahma appointed Chandrama as the ruler of all the Nakshatras, planets, Brahm"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6207" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-2-1" target="concept-sacrifice"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 17, "quote": "3.2.1 Description of Priyavrat’s Lineage Maitreya says- \"O sage! Now I wish to hear the description of the lineage of Priyavrata who was the son of Swayambhu Manu.\" Parashar says- Priyavrata was married to the daughter of sage Kard"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6208" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-2-4" target="concept-shiva"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 19, "quote": "3.2.4 Description of Other Dvipas Plakshdweep- Plakshdweep has an expansion of 2,00,000 Yojans. Its ruler Meghatithi had seven sons- Shaanthaya, Shishir, Sukhodaya, Anand, Shiva, Kshemak and Dhruv. Those seven princes later"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6209" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-2-10" target="concept-devi"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 23, "quote": "3.2.10 Description of Surya Shakti and Vaishnava Shakti Maitreya says- \"Lord, if only the seven Ganas are entrusted with the job of causing cold and summer, drought and rain, what is the purpose then of the Sun’s existence? \" Parashar says- It is"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6210" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-2-13" target="concept-sacrifice"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 26, "quote": "3.2.13 Jadabharat Preaches the King The king said-\"O Brahmin. I was going to see sage Kapil and have the preaching regarding excellent human virtues. But now, hearing your words, I feel that I need not go any further. You are"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6211" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-2-15" target="concept-sacrifice"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 26, "quote": "3.2.15 Ribhu Preaches Nidaagh One thousand years after this incident, Ribhu once again decided to see his disciple Nidaagh. So he once again arrived in Veernagar. At that time, king of that town was leading a procession"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6212" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-3-3" target="concept-vishnu"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 29, "quote": "3.3.3 Description of Veda Vyasa and the Significance of BrahmaGyana Maitreya says- \"O Lord! How did God divide Vedas in the form of Vedavyasa during different Yugas?\" Parashar says- During each Dwaparyug, in every Kalpa, Lord Vishnu takes incarnation as Veda"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6213" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-3-5" target="concept-sacrifice"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 29, "quote": "3.3.5 Description of the Branches of the Yajur Veda A disciple of Vedavyasa named Vaishampayan created twenty-seven branches of Yajurveda and taught them to his disciples. He had a disciple Yagyavalkya who was the son of Brahmarat. At that ti"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6214" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-3-8" target="concept-vishnu"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 31, "quote": "3.3.8 Duties of Four Classes of Society Maitreya says - \"Lord! How should one worship Lord Vishnu? Kindly describe it to me. Parashar says- King Sagar had asked the same thing from sage Aurv. I am narrating what sage Aurv had prea"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6215" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-3-8" target="concept-dharma"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 31, "quote": "3.3.8 Duties of Four Classes of Society Maitreya says - \"Lord! How should one worship Lord Vishnu? Kindly describe it to me. Parashar says- King Sagar had asked the same thing from sage Aurv. I am narrating what sage Aurv had prea"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6216" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-3-8" target="concept-sacrifice"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 31, "quote": "3.3.8 Duties of Four Classes of Society Maitreya says - \"Lord! How should one worship Lord Vishnu? Kindly describe it to me. Parashar says- King Sagar had asked the same thing from sage Aurv. I am narrating what sage Aurv had prea"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6217" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-3-11" target="concept-dharma"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 32, "quote": "3.3.11 Description of Righteousness A married man knows the importance of following a righteous discourse. Married life is like a penance in which a couple gives birth and raises next generation. A married man is expected to g"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6218" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-3-13" target="concept-shiva"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 33, "quote": "3.3.13 Days for Monthly Oblations A Shraadh carried out with devotion pleases the entire world including human beings, Brahma, Indra, Rudra, Ashwini Kumars, Surya, Agni, Vasugana, Marudgana, Vishwadeva, Pitragana, birds, ani"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6219" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-3-13" target="concept-devotion"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 33, "quote": "3.3.13 Days for Monthly Oblations A Shraadh carried out with devotion pleases the entire world including human beings, Brahma, Indra, Rudra, Ashwini Kumars, Surya, Agni, Vasugana, Marudgana, Vishwadeva, Pitragana, birds, ani"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6220" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-3-15" target="concept-sacrifice"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-1", "page": 34, "quote": "3.3.15 Do’s and Don’t during Oblation Oblation with flesh of fish, rabbit, mongoose, hog, deer, ram and cereals cause extreme satisfaction for the ancestors. But in modern Kaliyug, all types of flesh are forbidden in oblation ri"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6221" source="p-vishnu-puran-1-3-3-15" targe