ishnu to rescue them. Lord Vishnu told them that he"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6225" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-3-4-5" target="concept-sacrifice"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 2, "quote": "3.4.5 Tale of Nimi and Description of his Lineage Ikshvaku’s son Nimi once decided to organise a Yagya that was to last for one thousand years. He also wanted the sage Vashishta to guide the Yagya. But Indra had already booked Vashishta for"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6226" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-3-4-6" target="concept-sacrifice"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 3, "quote": "3.4.6 Description of Somavansh and the Tale of Pururava The creator of the world, Brahma had a son named Atri. Chandrama was the son of Atri. Once Chandrama organised a Rajsuya Yagya and received great powers. Afterwards blinded by his powers, Ch"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6227" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-3-4-11" target="concept-dharma"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 6, "quote": "3.4.11 Description of Yaduvansh and the Tale of SahastrArjuna Yayati’s eldest son Yadu had four sons- Sahastrajit, Kroshtu, Nala and Nahush. Sahastrajit had a son Shatajit who had three sons Haihaya, Hehaya and Venuhaya. Lineage of Haihaya grew as- Dha"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6228" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-3-5-4" target="concept-vishnu"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 9, "quote": "3.5.4 Appearance of Lord in Devaki’s Womb As per the dictate of Lord Vishnu, Yogamaaya implanted six foetuses in the womb of Devaki. All the six children were killed by Kansa immediately after their birth. Yogamaaya transplanted the"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6229" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-3-5-5" target="concept-moksha"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 10, "quote": "3.5.5 Killing of Putana and Salvation of other Demons When Vasudev was released from the prison, Nand visited Mathura on some official trip. He also came to see Vasudev. Vasudev greeted him for the birth of a son and instructed him to return to"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6230" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-11-297" target="concept-moksha"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 11, "quote": "SALVATION OF TRINAVART Once Mata Yashoda was playing with the baby lord in her home. All of a sudden she felt as if the baby was getting disproportionately heavy. Soon, she felt herself unable to bear the child an"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6231" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-11-1533" target="concept-sacrifice"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 11, "quote": "NAMING OF LORD KRISHNA Once, the supreme ascetic Gargacharya arrived in Gokul. He was the ancestral teacher of Yaduvanshis. Nand joyfully welcomed and treated the hermit. Then he requested him to carry out the rit"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6232" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-12-1241" target="concept-moksha"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 12, "quote": "UKHAL BANDHAN AND SALVATION OF YAMALARJUN Once, wishing to feed Krishna with butter, Yashoda began to churn milk in the morning. Very soon, Krishna too awakened and not finding the mother on her bed, He set out to search her. Soon H"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6233" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-12-3844" target="concept-shiva"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 12, "quote": "MIGRATION TO VRINDAVANA The uprooted Arjun trees fell with thundering sound. All the people shivered with fear and felt as if lightning had struck somewhere. All the elders including Nand met together and discussed"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6234" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-13-887" target="concept-moksha"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 13, "quote": "SALVATION OF VATSASUR One day, Balaram and Krishna were grazing their cattle on the bank of Yamuna River. A demon, meanwhile, took the guise of a calf and mixed with the herd. Obviously, he had malicious intentio"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6235" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-13-1522" target="concept-moksha"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 13, "quote": "SALVATION OF BAKASUR One day, all the cowherds took their cattle to a large pond to let them drink water. There they say a huge creature sitting like a hillock on the bank. They were frightened by its appearance"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6236" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-13-2423" target="concept-moksha"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 13, "quote": "SALVATION OF AGHASUR One day, Krishna planned a picnic near Nandanvan. So rising early in the morning, He awakened his fellow cowherds sounding a horn. Together, all the cowherds, and their cattle went to the fo"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6237" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-14-0" target="concept-moksha"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 14, "quote": "ATTACHMENT OF BRAHMA, STEALING OF CATTLE AND COWHERDS Parashar says: The cowherds told the tale of Aghasur's salvation to their parents only after a year of the incidence. During that period of one year, Lord Krishna multiplied himself and took"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6238" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-14-2154" target="concept-moksha"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 14, "quote": "SALVATION OF DHENUKASUR When Krishna and Balaram entered sixth year of their ages, they got the permission to take the cattle out for grazing. Along with their fellow cowherds the two brothers too began to take the"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6239" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-15-2460" target="concept-moksha"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 15, "quote": "SALVATION OF PRALAMBASUR One day, Balaram and Krishna were playfully grazing their cattle along with other cowherds in the forests. When a demon Pralamb arrived there with an intention of kidnapping Krishna and Bala"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6240" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-16-2782" target="concept-devi"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summa