ord Krishna and Balaram arrived in the amphi- theatre. The spectators present in the"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6252" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-23-1392" target="concept-moksha"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 23, "quote": "SALVATION OF KANSA Seeing the shameful defeat of his wrestlers, Kansa infuriated with anger and proclaimed: \"Tie all the opponents; tie Ugrasen, Devaki, Vasudev and Nand in ropes and bring them before me.\" Lor"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6253" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-27-1645" target="concept-shiva"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 27, "quote": "BIRTH OF PRADYUMN, KILLING OF SHABARASUR Kamadev was a part of lord himself. After getting incinerated by Rudra, Kamadev took refuge in the supreme lord to get an incarnation once more. Thus, Kamadev was born as Rukmani’s first son"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6254" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-27-2941" target="concept-vishnu"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 27, "quote": "TALE OF SYAMANTAK THE GEM A person named Satrajit was a great devotee of Lord Suryanarayana. Pleased by his devotion, Suryadev presented him a gem called Syamantak. The gem had radiance equal to the Sun. Bearing that"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6255" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-27-2941" target="concept-devotion"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 27, "quote": "TALE OF SYAMANTAK THE GEM A person named Satrajit was a great devotee of Lord Suryanarayana. Pleased by his devotion, Suryadev presented him a gem called Syamantak. The gem had radiance equal to the Sun. Bearing that"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6256" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-29-1184" target="concept-moksha"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 29, "quote": "LORD'S MARRIAGE WITH LAKSHMANA Lakshmana was the daughter of the king of Madra. She was very beautiful and meritorious. Lord abducted her all alone from the Swayamvara organised for her marriage. Later, Lord married to he"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6257" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-30-485" target="concept-shiva"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 30, "quote": "MARRIAGE OF USHA-ANIRUDH The son of the demon king Bali, Baanasur was a great devotee of Lord Shiva. Baanasur ruled over the kingdom Shonitpur. By the grace of Lord Shiva, he had received thousand arms. Even all the"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6258" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-30-485" target="concept-devotion"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 30, "quote": "MARRIAGE OF USHA-ANIRUDH The son of the demon king Bali, Baanasur was a great devotee of Lord Shiva. Baanasur ruled over the kingdom Shonitpur. By the grace of Lord Shiva, he had received thousand arms. Even all the"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6259" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-30-3074" target="concept-moksha"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 30, "quote": "SALVATION OF PAUNDRAK Once Balaram and Krishna had gone to Braj to see Nandbaba there. Meanwhile the king Paundrak of Karush sent an envoy to lord Krishna with a message that said: 'I am Lord Vasudev.' Pandrak's"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6260" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-31-1151" target="concept-moksha"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 31, "quote": "SALVATION OF DWIVID There was once a monkey named Dwivid. He was the friend of Bhaumasur. When Dwivid heard about Bhaumasur's killing by Shri Krishna, he began to cause large-scale destruction in the kingdom. H"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6261" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-32-505" target="concept-sacrifice"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 32, "quote": "KILLING OF JARASANDH During Yudhisthir’s Rajsuy Yagya, all the Pandavas set out in all the directions to conquer the kings and expand the boundaries of their kingdom. Warriors like Bheema, Arjun defeated great k"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6262" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-32-1849" target="concept-shiva"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "page": 32, "quote": "SALVATION OF SHISHUPAL King Yudhishthir had invited great Vedic Brahmins and Acharayas on the occasion. Persons from Kauravas side like Drona, Bheeshma, Kripacharya, Dhritarashtra, Vidur and Duryodhan etc. were to"}]</data></edge><edge id="e6263" source="p-vishnu-puran-2-upper-32-1849" target="concept-moksha"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "vishnu-puran-2", "pa