nique D. SUPINE POSTURES Bend both the legs at the knees and bring the heels near the buttocks. SETUBANDHASANA • While holding both the ankles firmly, keep the knees and feet i"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7018" source="b-yoga-page-39" target="concept-yoga"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "common-yoga-aasana-englishebook", "page": 39, "quote": "COMMON YOGA PROTOCOL Ministry of Ayush, Government of India UTTÂNAPÃDÃSANA Technique (Raised feet posture) Lie comfortably on the ground with the legs stretched out. Ottana means raised-upwards and Pada"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7019" source="b-yoga-page-40" target="concept-yoga"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "common-yoga-aasana-englishebook", "page": 40, "quote": "COMMON YOGA PROTOCOL Ministry of Ayush, Government of India ARDHAHALÃSANA (Half-Plough Posture) \"Ardha' means half and 'Hala' means plough. This posture is known as Ardhahalāsana because in its final position, the body would"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7020" source="b-yoga-page-41" target="concept-yoga"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "common-yoga-aasana-englishebook", "page": 41, "quote": "COMMON YOGA PROTOCOL Ministry of Ayush, Government of India PAVANAMUKTÃSANA (Wind-Releasing Posture) Pavana means wind and mukta means to release or to make free. As the name suggests, this sana is useful in removing wind or flatulence from"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7021" source="b-yoga-page-42" target="concept-yoga"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "common-yoga-aasana-englishebook", "page": 42, "quote": "COMMON YOGA PROTOCOL Ministry of Ayush, Government of India Technique SAVĂSANA Lie down on back with arms and legs comfortably apart. (Corpse/ Dead-Body Posture) Palms facing upwards, eyes closed."}]</data></edge><edge id="e7022" source="b-yoga-page-43" target="concept-yoga"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "common-yoga-aasana-englishebook", "page": 43, "quote": "COMMON YOGA PROTOCOL Ministry of Ayush, Government of India 4 KAPÃLABHÄTI Kapal means skull, bhati means to shine or to cleanse. It is a cleansing practice which helps to clean the frontal sinuses and upper respirating tract. Sthiti: Sukhās"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7023" source="b-yoga-page-44" target="concept-yoga"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "common-yoga-aasana-englishebook", "page": 44, "quote": "COMMON YOGA PROTOCOL Ministry of Ayush, Government of India Benefits This practice purifies the frontal air sinuses; helps to overcome cough disorders. • It is useful in treating cold, rhinitis, sinusitis, asthma, and bronchial infections."}]</data></edge><edge id="e7024" source="b-yoga-page-45" target="concept-yoga"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "common-yoga-aasana-englishebook", "page": 45, "quote": "COMMON YOGA PROTOCOL Ministry of Ayush, Government of India 5 PRĂNAYAMA NADISODHANA or ANULOMA VILOMA PRANÃYÃMA (Alternate Nostril Breathing) The main characteristic feature of this"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7025" source="b-yoga-page-46" target="concept-yoga"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "common-yoga-aasana-englishebook", "page": 46, "quote": "COMMON YOGA PROTOCOL Ministry of Ayush, Government of India • Gradually make the ratio 1:2 (inhalation:exhalation, respectively). Breathing Breath should be slow, steady, and controlled. It should not be forced or restricted in anyway."}]</data></edge><edge id="e7026" source="b-yoga-page-47" target="concept-yoga"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "common-yoga-aasana-englishebook", "page": 47, "quote": "COMMON YOGA PROTOCOL Ministry of Ayush, Government of India SITALİ PRANAYAMA Sitali means cooling. It also means calm and passionless. As the name indicates, this pranayāma cools the mind - and body. It is specially designed to reduce the b"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7027" source="b-yoga-page-48" target="concept-yoga"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "common-yoga-aasana-englishebook", "page": 48, "quote": "COMMON YOGA PROTOCOL Ministry of Ayush, Government of India Caution Those who are suffering from severe cold, cough or tonsillitis should not do this pranayama."}]</data></edge><edge id="e7028" source="b-yoga-page-49" target="concept-yoga"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "common-yoga-aasana-englishebook", "page": 49, "quote": "COMMON YOGA PROTOCOL Ministry of Ayush, Government of India BHRĂMARI PRĂNÂYÃMA Bhramari is derived from bhramara, which means black bee. During the practice of this pranayama, the sound produced resembles the buzzing of a black bee, hence"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7029" source="b-yoga-page-50" target="concept-yoga"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "common-yoga-aasana-englishebook", "page": 50, "quote": "COMMON YOGA PROTOCOL Ministry of Ayush, Government of India Benefits It relieves stress and helps in alleviating anxiety, anger, and hyper activity. It creates a soothing effect on the nervous system and mind. It is a great tranquiliser, an"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7030" source="b-yoga-page-51" target="concept-yoga"><data key="type">theme</data><data key="summary">Editorial theme tag on this indexed entry; compare the source in context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "common-yoga-aasana-englishebook", "page": 51, "quote": "COMMON YOGA PROTOCOL Ministry of Ayush, Government of Iridia 6 DHYÃNA Dhyana or meditation is an act of continuous contemplation. Sthiti: Any comfortable posture. Technique"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7031" source="concept-agni" target="doc-practical-vastu-professional-guide-1"><data key="type">mentions</data><data key="summary">Literal name/term matches on 3 PDF pages; includes front matter and commentary where present. Search the source to inspect context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "practical-vastu-professional-guide-1", "page": 3, "quote": ", Lakshmi tattva, Agni respect and daily order. Core principles Vastu Purusha Mandala, Pancha Mahabhu"}, {"doc": "practical-vastu-professional-guide-1", "page": 4, "quote": "ms. maintained by discipline. Agni respect Kitchen fire handled cleanly and safely. Heat belongs in a controlled"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7032" source="concept-agni" target="doc-agni-puranas"><data key="type">mentions</data><data key="summary">Literal name/term matches on 11 PDF pages; includes front matter and commentary where present. Search the source to inspect context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "agni-puranas", "page": 1, "quote": "10 Agni Purana This Purana is basically a preaching to the sage Vashishth by Agni. In his turn, Vashishth narrated it"}, {"doc": "agni-puranas", "page": 7,