": "kurma-puran", "page": 17, "quote": "ra gave him a resounding kick and sent him reeling. The fire-god Agni had his arms and tongue sliced off by Virabhadra’s companions. The sages were kicked and boxed. Vishnu himse"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7036" source="concept-agni" target="doc-linga-purana"><data key="type">mentions</data><data key="summary">Literal name/term matches on 2 PDF pages; includes front matter and commentary where present. Search the source to inspect context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "linga-purana", "page": 2, "quote": "rd tanmantra, form or roopa originated from air or Yayu. Fire or Agni manifested from roopa. The fourth tanmantra, taste or rasa manifested from Agni. Similarly, water or Jal man"}, {"doc": "linga-purana", "page": 3, "quote": "aksh, Raj, Suhotra, Bahu, Nishpaap, Shravan, Tapasvi and Shukra. Agni's consort Swaha gave birth to three sons-Pavamaan, Paavak and Shuchi. 17.1.4 Lord Shiva – The Supreme Libera"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7037" source="concept-agni" target="doc-markandeya-puran"><data key="type">mentions</data><data key="summary">Literal name/term matches on 7 PDF pages; includes front matter and commentary where present. Search the source to inspect context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "markandeya-puran", "page": 27, "quote": "op the earth from swinging. But the mountains were burnt down by Agni (fire) named Samvartak. The mountains submerged into the ocean. The mountains after having displaced the wate"}, {"doc": "markandeya-puran", "page": 30, "quote": "Sutapa and Shukra. These seven are famous as the Saptarishis.' 'Agni was married to Swaha. Three sons were born to them- Paavak, Pavaman and Shuchi.' 7.9 The Various Manavantars"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7038" source="concept-agni" target="doc-matsyapurana-english"><data key="type">mentions</data><data key="summary">Literal name/term matches on 39 PDF pages; includes front matter and commentary where present. Search the source to inspect context.</data