reatness of Lord Shiva and propagation of Ling-puja (worship of Shiva-Ling) are the main objectives of this Purana. This Purana has"}, {"doc": "linga-purana", "page": 2, "quote": "Shiva is both invisible as well as the root cause of all the delusions of the world. This is why Shiva is also know"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7176" source="concept-shiva" target="doc-markandeya-puran"><data key="type">mentions</data><data key="summary">Literal name/term matches on 5 PDF pages; includes front matter and commentary where present. Search the source to inspect context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "markandeya-puran", "page": 14, "quote": ", Kambal became famous singers. Then they began worshipping Lord Shiva singing sweet and melodious hymns. Pleased by their prayers, Lord Shankar also asked them to seek a boon. At"}, {"doc": "markandeya-puran", "page": 15, "quote": "Bowing before Lord Shiva thereafter, both the brothers returned to their kingdom in Paatal loka. Ashwatar organised a Shraadh in the s"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7177" source="concept-shiva" target="doc-matsyapurana-english"><data key="type">mentions</data><data key="summary">Literal name/term matches on 134 PDF pages; includes front matter and commentary where present. Search the source to inspect context.</data><data key="evidence">[{"doc": "matsyapurana-english", "page": 19, "quote": "formed by the letters a, u, m. Of these, a representa Vienu, u, Siva, m, Brahma. Pranava is, therefore, the symbol of the sacred Trinity. CHAPTER I May the lotus feet of Bhava, w"}, {"doc": "matsyapurana-english", "page": 20, "quote": "e couplet \"Prachand Tandavâtope, eto., contains a prayer to Lord siva which shows that later on there will be something about the annihilation of the universe. siva is Sanhârkarta"}]</data></edge><edge id="e7178" source="concept-shiva" target="doc-narad-puran"><data key="type">mentions</data><data key="summary">Literal name/term matches on 6 PDF pages; includes front matter and commentary w